From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Golmann <mail@pje-web.de>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:38:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] modem-helpers: accept two-digit AcT values in +CREG, +CGREG
 and +CEREG

Description: Accept two-digit AcT values in +CREG, +CGREG and +CEREG
 The registration patterns only accepted a one-digit AcT field, so AcT 10-13
 (5G core and NR) lines matched nothing. A modem that registers on 5G SA after
 ModemManager's registration attempt has stopped polling stays in 'searching',
 because its registered URCs are dropped and no periodic check runs while
 unsolicited registration reports are enabled. Also reads the +CREG/+CGREG
 <lac> as a TAC on NR.
 .
 Not offered upstream yet. The same change applies to upstream main, which
 still accepts one AcT digit in these patterns.
Author: Paul Golmann <mail@pje-web.de>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-25

27.007 defines AcT 10 (E-UTRA connected to a 5GCN), 11 (NR connected to a
5GCN), 12 (NG-RAN) and 13 (E-UTRA-NR dual connectivity), and
get_mm_access_tech_from_etsi_access_tech() already maps them. The +CREG,
+CGREG and +CEREG patterns that carry an AcT field only accept one digit
there, so a line such as

  +CEREG: 1,"1F00","12345A00B",11

matches none of them. Only +C5GREG and the six-field +CGREG layout with a
trailing RAC accepted two digits.

The Fibocom FM350-GL reports its 5G SA registration this way. Its
searching answers (AcT 0) parse and its registered ones (AcT 11) don't,
so registered URCs are dropped. Periodic registration checks only run
when unsolicited reports can't be enabled, so once ModemManager's own
registration attempt has stopped polling, nothing reads the registration
again. After a replug on a US 5G SA network the module had registered on
NR while ModemManager reported 'searching' for four minutes; one
--3gpp-register-home made it read the registration.

Accept the four two-digit values, unpadded, in the AcT field of those
patterns. Padded or other values keep failing, so a padded cell id or an
unquoted RAC is not read as an AcT, and [7] takes a two-digit AcT only
after an unpadded <stat>; this keeps "+CGREG: 1,0005,2816,3,11" on [9].
Also take the <lac> of +CREG and +CGREG as a TAC on NR, where there are
no location areas, so the three reports agree on the TAC.

The tests cover the FM350-GL layouts (quoted TAC, 36-bit NR cell id, the
RAC field in +CGREG), AcT 10 and 13, two replayed sequences and two
layouts a looser pattern would misread, each in forward order and in the
reverse order the AT port tries URC handlers. TAC and cell id values are
synthetic.
---
 src/mm-broadband-modem.c       |  18 +-
 src/mm-modem-helpers.c         |  34 +++-
 src/mm-modem-helpers.h         |   5 +
 src/tests/test-modem-helpers.c | 307 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 354 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

